-04-13T16:57:58Z","closed_at":"2026-04-13T16:47:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6 stable (mono)\n\n### System information\n\nN/A, but Windows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nI asked in a Godot discord server whether this was a bug, they explained it to me that it was not, but they recommended me that I might report it anyways as it might look confusing to others as well.\n\nMy initial thought was that the top -6 dB was supposed to be +6 dB, as when I slide it up, the value in the tooltip shows +6 dB\n\nThey then explained that it's just a reference range, and then it clicked.\nThe 'second' negative 6 dB is actually the positive value, but happens to be on the reference line making it look like another -6 dB, as the reference dash/line is almost identical as the actual -6.0dB label\n\nI hope I didn't make it more confusing, basically it looks like there's two -6.0dB's on there\n\n<img width=\"142\" height=\"351\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed037b86-5fad-4ec4-81ff-95687455263b\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nJust look in audio level in any new project\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.